1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,771
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:30,113
[Emilia] <i>Dead people belong to this grave.</i>

6
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:31,740
<i>And you are dead.</i>

7
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:33,033
<i>Where did that come from?!</i>

8
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:35,243
<i>I don't want to see that!</i>
<i>Get that away from me!</i>

9
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:37,287
<i>Do you realize the mess</i>
<i>you're getting into?</i>

10
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:39,873
<i>I'm not scared,</i>
<i>because I know someone powerful.</i>

11
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:43,334
<i>More powerful than that politician</i>
<i>you're protecting!</i>

12
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:47,922
[Julio] <i>Who else dared to go against me?</i>

13
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:49,340
<i>Lily Cruz.</i>

14
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:52,177
<i>I want you to hunt down Lily Cruz.</i>

15
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:55,096
<i>I want her dead. Do you understand me?</i>

16
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:56,765
[Jepoy] <i>If your life was in danger before,</i>

17
00:00:56,848 --> 00:00:58,099
<i>then it's even more so now.</i>

18
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:00,643
<i>What are you going to do now?</i>
<i>Jump off this cliff?</i>

19
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:02,353
<i>Or would you rather get shot?</i>

20
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:05,148
[man] <i>No one could survive</i>
<i>falling from that height!</i>

21
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:08,735
[Julio] <i>Don't forget the people</i>
<i>who did this to you.</i>

22
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:12,363
<i>Use that hate so that you may rise</i>

23
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:15,408
<i>and rule by my side once again.</i>

24
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:16,951
[Camia] <i>How did your meeting go?</i>

25
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:19,662
[Diego] <i>I am hoping that the</i>
<i>vice governor won't let us down.</i>

26
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:20,663
<i>Don't worry, Aunt Camia.</i>

27
00:01:20,747 --> 00:01:23,958
<i>I'll do whatever it takes</i>
<i>to finish Lily's fight.</i>

28
00:01:24,042 --> 00:01:24,876
<i>We can do this.</i>

29
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,503
[man] This is from the governor.

30
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:28,797
[Leandro] <i>Tell Governor Ardiente</i>

31
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:30,507
<i>that I'm looking forward</i>
<i>to his celebration.</i>

32
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:33,218
[Julio] <i>Citizens of Ardiente!</i>

33
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:37,931
<i>We invite all of you</i>
<i>to join us in the celebration</i>

34
00:01:38,014 --> 00:01:42,602
<i>of our province's one-hundredth year!</i>

35
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:44,354
[crowd cheering]

36
00:01:46,105 --> 00:01:49,442
-[festive music playing]
-[man] Viva Ardiente!

37
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:51,653
[festive music playing]

38
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:53,238
[man] Viva Ardiente!

39
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:59,077
[festive music continues]

40
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:02,288
HAPPY CENTENNIAL ANNIVERSARY,
POBLACION ARDIENTE!

41
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:07,335
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente!

42
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:10,964
[woman] Long live, Ardiente!

43
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:16,427
[marching band playing]

44
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:33,862
[marching band playing]

45
00:02:47,041 --> 00:02:51,045
[marching band playing]

46
00:03:04,642 --> 00:03:08,730
[marching band playing]

47
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:21,159
[marching band playing]

48
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:38,843
[marching band playing]

49
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:51,981
[marching band playing]

50
00:04:02,158 --> 00:04:06,120
[marching band playing]

51
00:04:17,215 --> 00:04:19,759
[marching band playing]

52
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:23,680
[crowd] Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

53
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:27,392
They will still bow down to the king.

54
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:29,978
[tense music playing]

55
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:35,066
I still have Poblacion Ardiente
wrapped around my finger.

56
00:04:36,192 --> 00:04:40,238
[tense music playing]

57
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:49,372
[woman 1] Viva! Viva Ardiente!

58
00:04:50,581 --> 00:04:53,960
[woman 2] Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

59
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:59,507
[crowd] Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

60
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:02,051
[woman squealing]

61
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:07,890
[crowd chanting] Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

62
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:09,309
[Julio] Hi!

63
00:05:11,811 --> 00:05:14,397
-[woman 3] Happy fiesta!
-[Julio] Thank you!

64
00:05:16,274 --> 00:05:19,402
[music swells]

65
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:25,616
Remember, we're attending the celebration

66
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:28,036
not to cause trouble or to protest.

67
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:31,831
We're still citizens
of Poblacion Ardiente.

68
00:05:31,914 --> 00:05:35,710
We have the right to join in
the festivities of our province.

69
00:05:35,793 --> 00:05:37,128
-Right!
-[all] That's right!

70
00:05:37,211 --> 00:05:39,213
-All right!
-[Camia] Right, Loring?

71
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:40,882
That's right So let's go.

72
00:05:40,965 --> 00:05:41,883
-Let's go.
-Yes.

73
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:45,053
-[Camia] All right.
-[Loring] Come on.

74
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:49,015
Um…

75
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:52,977
Can't you just stay behind?

76
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:54,812
Why, Damian?

77
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:56,606
You might get into trouble out there.

78
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,649
No, I won't.

79
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:00,318
[inhales sharply]

80
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:02,403
Camia, in case you've forgotten,

81
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:05,239
you're the only one left in your family.

82
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:08,367
Damian, if Dante were still alive,

83
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:09,911
he'd go there too.

84
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:14,040
And that's the reason he
and your daughter are gone now.

85
00:06:14,123 --> 00:06:15,792
I'm ready to lay down my life

86
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:17,710
for the people of Poblacion Ardiente.

87
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:20,254
That's what Lily believed in

88
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:22,256
and that's what I believe in too.

89
00:06:22,965 --> 00:06:25,384
But are they ready to do the same for you?

90
00:06:25,843 --> 00:06:28,805
-That's not important anymore.
-To you, it's not.

91
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:32,225
[sighs] But to me, it is.

92
00:06:32,683 --> 00:06:34,977
Dante's greatest mistake was forgetting

93
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:36,604
his responsibilities to you
as your husband.

94
00:06:36,687 --> 00:06:39,107
It was his responsibility
to take care of you and Lily,

95
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:41,275
not to give justice to other people.

96
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:43,152
But I chose this.

97
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:44,403
That's what you think, Camia,

98
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:46,697
because you feel that no one's
taking care of you.

99
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:47,824
-And that's--
-Damian…

100
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:50,368
Dante loved me.

101
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:53,121
But not in the way you deserve.

102
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:55,915
What do you mean by that?

103
00:06:59,168 --> 00:07:00,253
Nothing.

104
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,630
[sighs] Nothing.

105
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:05,341
All right.

106
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:07,135
Just be careful out there.

107
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:20,773
[somber music playing]

108
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:31,409
Commissioner, someone
wants to talk with you.

109
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:33,453
Didn't I tell you to cancel
all my appointments?

110
00:07:33,536 --> 00:07:35,455
I'm going to Poblacion Ardiente, remember?

111
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:39,584
-He says it's urgent.
-Commissioner, we need to talk.

112
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:44,046
Mr. Torillo, I rejected your appeal

113
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,923
because it lacks evidence.

114
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:48,384
If I were you, I'd just accept defeat.

115
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:52,221
Commissioner, I didn't come here for that.

116
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:54,348
[tense music playing]

117
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:55,433
Then what?

118
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:03,816
[ominous music playing]

119
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:20,666
I'm sorry, but you
aren't allowed to enter.

120
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,084
-What?
-Why not?

121
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:24,253
We live in Poblacion Ardiente.

122
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:26,380
We are residents of this town too.

123
00:08:26,464 --> 00:08:27,924
I'm sorry, but you're not on the list.

124
00:08:28,216 --> 00:08:31,636
What list? This one?
You haven't even checked it yet.

125
00:08:31,719 --> 00:08:33,179
How'd you know we're not on it?

126
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:35,806
[Julio] Excuse me, excuse me. Hold on.

127
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:40,520
You are not allowed
to enter here, because…

128
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:44,273
You're not. [chuckles]

129
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:50,488
Your attire does not fit
the motif of the party.

130
00:08:50,738 --> 00:08:52,865
But we're residents
of Poblacion Ardiente too.

131
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:55,493
-[man 1] That's right.
-Oh. I got news for you, girl.

132
00:08:55,826 --> 00:08:59,956
Not for long. Not for long.

133
00:09:00,706 --> 00:09:03,793
Sanggano, if these people
insist on coming in,

134
00:09:04,001 --> 00:09:06,045
-feel free to arrest them.
-Yes, Governor.

135
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:08,172
-[man 2] This old man!
-I love to be in power.

136
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:10,258
-Not for long?
-We dressed up for nothing.

137
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:12,426
We'll see about that.

138
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:16,639
[tense music playing]

139
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:22,645
[host] Let's all give
a warm round of applause

140
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:25,940
for the Ardiente family!

141
00:09:26,023 --> 00:09:30,027
[crowd applauding, cheering]

142
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:38,327
[marching band playing]

143
00:09:55,428 --> 00:10:00,474
[marching band playing]

144
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:16,782
[marching band playing]

145
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:42,850
[marching band playing]

146
00:10:45,603 --> 00:10:50,733
[crowd chanting]
Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

147
00:10:50,816 --> 00:10:52,360
Viva Ardiente!

148
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:56,113
[music fading]

149
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:01,285
Governor, the area is secure.

150
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:05,873
Okay. I just got word
that Secretary Martel

151
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:08,668
is near Ardiente already.

152
00:11:09,126 --> 00:11:12,963
So I want you to ready our men
and meet him at the arch.

153
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:17,468
He's your number one priority
as far as security is concerned.

154
00:11:17,551 --> 00:11:19,553
Convoy him on the way here.

155
00:11:20,012 --> 00:11:21,305
-Yes, Governor.
-Okay.

156
00:11:22,139 --> 00:11:23,974
[host] Good evening, everyone.

157
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:27,895
Let us begin our grand celebration.

158
00:11:27,978 --> 00:11:30,064
And for the opening remarks,

159
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:32,775
let us give a round of applause
for our former governor.

160
00:11:32,858 --> 00:11:35,569
Our one and only best friend…

161
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:38,864
Mrs. Emilia Ardiente-Torillo!

162
00:11:39,323 --> 00:11:44,286
-[crowd applauding]
-[marching band playing]

163
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:55,631
Hello, friends!

164
00:11:55,714 --> 00:11:59,885
And to everyone,
a warm welcome to you all!

165
00:12:00,094 --> 00:12:02,430
This night is a very special one

166
00:12:02,513 --> 00:12:08,269
because it is the celebration
of our province's centennial!

167
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:09,645
Congratulations to us.

168
00:12:09,728 --> 00:12:12,022
-Viva Ardiente!
-[crowd applauding]

169
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:14,650
-[crowd] Viva Ardiente!
-[applauding]

170
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:19,071
But this isn't just
a celebration of our town.

171
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:23,409
It is also a celebration
of the return of someone

172
00:12:23,492 --> 00:12:26,078
very dear to my heart and yours too.

173
00:12:26,745 --> 00:12:29,623
Someone who gave his life,

174
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:31,000
his time,

175
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:33,961
and his whole heart for our province.

176
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:40,134
The one you all chose to lead our people.

177
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:43,053
Let us give a round of applause
for my father,

178
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:46,307
Governor Julio Ardiente!

179
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:50,394
[crowd applauding, cheering]

180
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:06,660
Papa, we have a surprise for you
and for everyone here tonight.

181
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:10,706
Let us all welcome,
the talented Ardiente Dancers!

182
00:13:10,789 --> 00:13:13,334
-[applauding]
-[metal drums clanging]

183
00:13:15,085 --> 00:13:19,215
[chiming musically]

184
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:42,571
[tribal music continues]

185
00:13:55,251 --> 00:13:59,255
[tribal music continues]

186
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:17,523
[tribal music continues]

187
00:14:20,109 --> 00:14:24,113
[ominous music playing]

188
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:35,958
[tribal music continues]

189
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:56,812
[tribal music continues]

190
00:15:19,835 --> 00:15:23,881
[tribal music continues]

191
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:30,304
[ominous music playing]

192
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,440
[tribal music continues]

193
00:15:52,117 --> 00:15:56,705
[tribal music continues]

194
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:03,587
[music stops]

195
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:11,512
[upbeat tribal music playing]

196
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:24,942
[ominous music playing]

197
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:37,037
Ma'am, someone asked me to give you this.

198
00:16:37,121 --> 00:16:39,289
-Huh? From who?
-This is for you.

199
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:40,374
They didn't say.

200
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:42,209
[crowd applauding]

201
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:46,380
-[phone ringing]
-[suspenseful music playing]

202
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:49,883
[Emilia] <i>Aren't you glad</i>
<i>I left that little cell phone</i>

203
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:51,635
inside that casket?

204
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:53,929
And you have me for company.

205
00:16:54,388 --> 00:16:55,764
[phone continues ringing]

206
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:58,934
[host] Let's give the Ardiente Dancers
a round of applause!

207
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:00,769
-[crowd applauding]
-[phone continues ringing]

208
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:04,648
[host] And now, I'd like to call
on our vice governor

209
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:09,028
to recognize the honorable
citizens of Ardiente.

210
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:12,614
-[crowd applauding]
-[suspenseful music playing]

211
00:17:16,076 --> 00:17:19,747
[phone continues ringing]

212
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:25,753
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[phone continues ringing]

213
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:31,884
-[phone continues ringing]
-No.

214
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:35,345
[phone continues ringing]

215
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:37,848
No… This can't be happening.

216
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:40,100
-[phone continues ringing]
-No.

217
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:43,937
[phone continues ringing]

218
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:48,108
Hello?

219
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,069
<i>Hello, Emilia.</i>

220
00:17:50,569 --> 00:17:52,571
[suspenseful music playing]

221
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:56,950
No… This is impossible.
This is not happening.

222
00:17:57,034 --> 00:18:00,954
<i>Was it really impossible</i>
<i>to hear from me again, Emilia?</i>

223
00:18:01,038 --> 00:18:04,500
Yes, because I heard
your last breath, Ivy!

224
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:06,251
You're dead!

225
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:12,257
<i>You're right, Emilia. Ivy Aguas is dead.</i>

226
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:14,051
No…

227
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:16,804
This is not happ-- No.

228
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:17,971
[gasps]

229
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:22,017
How--

230
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:24,478
[breathing heavily]

231
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:29,733
[breathing heavily]

232
00:18:30,275 --> 00:18:31,151
Emilia?

233
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:33,487
Oh.

234
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:34,905
Raul.

235
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:39,451
Are you okay? What are you doing here?

236
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:42,871
[voice shaking] Nothing.
Just getting some fresh air.

237
00:18:43,872 --> 00:18:47,459
[tense music playing]

238
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:49,461
Okay. Let's go?

239
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:56,885
We would like to thank
Vice Governor Mateo Ruiz,

240
00:18:56,969 --> 00:19:00,097
and the veterans of Poblacion Ardiente.

241
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,473
Let's give them a round of applause!

242
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:05,644
[crowd cheering, applauding]

243
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:10,482
And now, I know everyone's
excited to hear his message.

244
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:12,401
Without further ado,

245
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:17,030
let's call on our province's
beloved father.

246
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:21,785
Give it up for Governor Julio Ardiente!

247
00:19:21,869 --> 00:19:25,914
-[march band playing]
-[crowd cheering, applauding]

248
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:45,267
[crowd] Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

249
00:19:46,935 --> 00:19:49,771
-Thank you very much, everyone.
-[camera shutters clicking]

250
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:53,275
Fellow citizens of Ardiente,

251
00:19:53,942 --> 00:20:00,699
it's so heartwarming to see your
overwhelming love and support

252
00:20:00,782 --> 00:20:02,284
for this humble servant.

253
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:06,330
I know none of this would've
been possible…

254
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:10,292
without your trust in me.

255
00:20:10,709 --> 00:20:14,922
So, in return,
I will promise you one thing…

256
00:20:17,674 --> 00:20:22,137
If anyone dares to take
this province for themselves…

257
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:26,099
Or you, my children, for that matter…

258
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:31,980
I will make sure that they answer to me.

259
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:35,442
[crowd cheering, applauding]

260
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:37,986
-[crowd] Viva Ardiente!
-[Julio] Viva Ardiente!

261
00:20:38,862 --> 00:20:43,575
I will not allow anyone
to waltz into this province

262
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:45,869
and take my family away from me.

263
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:49,790
The reason we won over our rivals

264
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:54,670
is that we're united as one family.

265
00:20:54,753 --> 00:20:58,215
[crowd applauding]

266
00:21:00,425 --> 00:21:06,890
And if ever my enemies and detractors

267
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:10,978
accuse me of doing things
I've never committed,

268
00:21:12,312 --> 00:21:14,314
I will not be fazed.

269
00:21:15,023 --> 00:21:20,696
Because the truth will always,
without a doubt, prevail!

270
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:25,284
[crowd cheering, applauding]

271
00:21:26,868 --> 00:21:31,415
[tense music playing]

272
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:36,044
Viva Ardiente!

273
00:21:36,128 --> 00:21:38,213
[all] Viva Ardiente!

274
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:41,174
[lights flick]

275
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:43,093
-[crowd exclaiming]
-[Julio] What happened?

276
00:21:43,176 --> 00:21:45,762
[crowd exclaiming]

277
00:21:46,388 --> 00:21:47,306
What's going on?

278
00:21:48,307 --> 00:21:49,308
What?

279
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:53,895
[ominous music playing]

280
00:22:04,948 --> 00:22:09,453
[ominous music continues]

281
00:22:20,714 --> 00:22:21,798
Lilies?

282
00:22:22,632 --> 00:22:26,636
[ominous music continues]

283
00:22:29,765 --> 00:22:34,770
[foreboding music playing]

284
00:22:47,991 --> 00:22:51,620
[indistinct shouting]

285
00:22:56,750 --> 00:23:01,630
[suspenseful music playing]

286
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:18,396
[smoke hissing]

287
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:26,363
[suspenseful music playing]

288
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:31,201
[smoke hissing continues]

289
00:23:41,962 --> 00:23:46,466
[suspenseful music playing]

290
00:24:02,649 --> 00:24:05,986
[epic action music playing]

291
00:24:08,155 --> 00:24:13,660
[suspenseful music playing]

292
00:24:18,081 --> 00:24:20,625
[woman 1] Ivy! It's Ivy!

293
00:24:21,334 --> 00:24:24,337
[indistinct crowd chatter]

294
00:24:28,049 --> 00:24:32,304
[epic action music playing]

295
00:24:32,387 --> 00:24:33,513
[explodes]

296
00:24:33,597 --> 00:24:35,307
[crowd exclaiming]

297
00:24:42,647 --> 00:24:44,149
[explodes]

298
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:51,656
[epic action music continues]

299
00:24:57,120 --> 00:24:58,580
[explodes]

300
00:25:03,668 --> 00:25:08,173
[epic action music continues]

301
00:25:17,098 --> 00:25:21,561
[tense music playing]

302
00:25:23,563 --> 00:25:24,773
[inaudible]

303
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,526
You're not real.

304
00:25:29,694 --> 00:25:33,490
Because you're dead, Ivy Aguas!
You're dead!

305
00:25:33,573 --> 00:25:37,035
Yes, Ivy Aguas is dead.

306
00:25:37,118 --> 00:25:41,206
Ivy Aguas is dead.

307
00:25:42,457 --> 00:25:44,751
But Lily Cruz…

308
00:25:44,834 --> 00:25:46,920
[ominous music playing]

309
00:25:47,003 --> 00:25:48,630
…is very much alive!

310
00:25:48,713 --> 00:25:50,757
[man 1] Lily Cruz? How did that happen?

311
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:52,592
-[woman 2] Isn't she dead?
-[man 2] Lily Cruz is alive?

312
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:57,722
[crowd chatter indistinctly]

313
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:05,730
Lily Cruz isn't dead.

314
00:26:06,398 --> 00:26:09,067
I am Lily Cruz.

315
00:26:09,150 --> 00:26:11,027
-[tense music playing]
-[crowd gasping]

316
00:26:11,111 --> 00:26:14,406
I am the real Lily Cruz!

317
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:17,242
And this time, you Ardientes

318
00:26:17,951 --> 00:26:20,161
will be the ones this town will mourn for.

319
00:26:21,496 --> 00:26:26,334
And starting tonight, at this very moment,

320
00:26:26,418 --> 00:26:29,129
you will finally lose all your power!

321
00:26:30,297 --> 00:26:33,216
Others may cry for you, but not me.

322
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:36,136
I will never, ever shed a tear.

323
00:26:36,219 --> 00:26:38,513
That's why I'm not wearing black.

324
00:26:39,055 --> 00:26:41,057
'Cause black is out!

325
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:42,809
Gold is in!

326
00:26:43,476 --> 00:26:49,357
Yes, just like gold, I am indestructible!

327
00:26:49,899 --> 00:26:54,404
[epic action music playing]

328
00:27:04,956 --> 00:27:08,960
[epic action music continues]

329
00:27:11,087 --> 00:27:14,174
[clock ticking]

330
00:27:14,257 --> 00:27:16,843
[gasping]

331
00:27:17,344 --> 00:27:19,054
[coughs, gasps]

332
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:21,681
[panting]

333
00:27:21,765 --> 00:27:23,266
<i>Ivy, hold on!</i>

334
00:27:24,392 --> 00:27:25,602
[screams]

335
00:27:27,771 --> 00:27:31,900
[somber music playing]

336
00:27:32,650 --> 00:27:35,612
[water trickling in distance]

337
00:27:37,530 --> 00:27:39,532
[grunting]

338
00:27:45,538 --> 00:27:47,999
[water trickling]

339
00:27:49,584 --> 00:27:53,213
[suspenseful music playing]

340
00:27:56,633 --> 00:27:57,634
-[thumps]
-[grunts]

341
00:28:00,678 --> 00:28:03,681
-[grunting]
-[thumping]

342
00:28:07,477 --> 00:28:09,187
-[grunting]
-[thumping]

343
00:28:13,108 --> 00:28:17,070
[suspenseful music playing]

344
00:28:17,737 --> 00:28:18,655
[wood breaking]

345
00:28:28,331 --> 00:28:31,334
[water trickling in distance]

346
00:28:34,587 --> 00:28:37,507
[Lily coughing]

347
00:28:40,385 --> 00:28:42,011
[coughing continues]

348
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:47,058
[gunshots]

349
00:28:47,767 --> 00:28:48,893
[henchman] <i>After them!</i>

350
00:28:51,104 --> 00:28:54,566
[gunshots]

351
00:28:55,608 --> 00:28:59,946
[Lily coughing, gasping]

352
00:29:05,660 --> 00:29:06,536
<i>Lily!</i>

353
00:29:07,287 --> 00:29:09,247
[groaning]

354
00:29:10,999 --> 00:29:13,501
[ominous music playing]

355
00:29:14,335 --> 00:29:16,880
<i>Lily… Lily, wake up!</i>

356
00:29:17,297 --> 00:29:19,299
-<i>Lily, wake up!</i>
-[groaning]

357
00:29:24,137 --> 00:29:25,138
<i>Lily!</i>

358
00:29:26,723 --> 00:29:28,933
[Marlon] <i>Be on the lookout!</i>
<i>You, check that area!</i>

359
00:29:29,017 --> 00:29:33,938
[somber music playing]

360
00:29:45,575 --> 00:29:46,659
<i>Ivy?</i>

361
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:51,080
<i>Diego! Jepoy!</i>

362
00:29:51,164 --> 00:29:52,499
<i>Ivy's over here!</i>

363
00:29:53,291 --> 00:29:57,003
<i>Jepoy, Diego… Marlon's calling!</i>

364
00:29:57,086 --> 00:29:59,339
-[Jepoy] <i>What?</i>
-<i>He found Ivy!</i>

365
00:30:04,302 --> 00:30:07,889
[suspenseful music playing]

366
00:30:12,101 --> 00:30:13,269
[Julio] You're too late.

367
00:30:14,270 --> 00:30:18,775
You're too late, Ivy Aguas--
or Lily Cruz, whoever you are.

368
00:30:19,359 --> 00:30:22,529
Dead or alive, you're too late.

369
00:30:22,862 --> 00:30:28,910
Because I've been declared
governor of Ardiente!

370
00:30:29,202 --> 00:30:32,622
I am Julio Ardiente…

371
00:30:32,705 --> 00:30:34,624
and this is my province.

372
00:30:39,212 --> 00:30:41,714
Martel! I'm glad you could make it.

373
00:30:42,382 --> 00:30:47,053
Tell everyone here who the real king of--

374
00:30:47,136 --> 00:30:48,221
[Diego] Julio Ardiente!

375
00:30:49,264 --> 00:30:52,267
[tense music playing]

376
00:30:52,559 --> 00:30:54,269
I believe this is your money.

377
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:58,106
The money you used
to bribe Secretary Martel!

378
00:30:58,189 --> 00:31:02,819
-[crowd murmuring]
-[tense music playing]

379
00:31:03,653 --> 00:31:06,656
You're fighting a losing battle,
Julio Ardiente.

380
00:31:08,032 --> 00:31:12,954
This is justice served
by the hand of Lily Cruz.

381
00:31:13,037 --> 00:31:14,873
[tense music playing]

382
00:31:15,206 --> 00:31:19,502
This is justice for Poblacion Ardiente!

383
00:31:19,586 --> 00:31:20,920
[woman 4] Goodness.

384
00:31:21,004 --> 00:31:24,507
[Lily] No matter how high you've
exalted yourself,

385
00:31:24,591 --> 00:31:26,050
I, Lily Cruz,

386
00:31:26,134 --> 00:31:29,262
will drag you down
to where you truly belong!

387
00:31:29,345 --> 00:31:31,556
[suspenseful music playing]

388
00:31:32,140 --> 00:31:33,683
[police] Governor Julio Ardiente,

389
00:31:33,766 --> 00:31:35,810
we have a warrant for your arrest

390
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:38,479
for the attempted murder of Camia Cruz.

391
00:31:38,563 --> 00:31:40,231
[suspenseful music continues]

392
00:31:40,315 --> 00:31:41,399
What?

393
00:31:41,816 --> 00:31:42,859
[inaudible]

394
00:31:44,110 --> 00:31:46,362
You can't do this to me!

395
00:31:46,446 --> 00:31:49,657
I am Julio Ardiente!

396
00:31:49,741 --> 00:31:51,200
I suggest you come with us, sir.

397
00:31:54,746 --> 00:31:56,456
-No… No!
-Don't touch me!

398
00:31:56,539 --> 00:31:59,500
[tense music playing]

399
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:02,879
Why don't you arrest this fraud instead--

400
00:32:03,546 --> 00:32:06,549
[foreboding music playing]

401
00:32:06,966 --> 00:32:08,968
[thuds]

402
00:32:11,721 --> 00:32:13,014
Papa!

403
00:32:15,099 --> 00:32:17,060
[suspenseful music playing]

404
00:32:17,143 --> 00:32:18,186
[cracks]

405
00:32:20,104 --> 00:32:22,148
-[crowd exclaiming]
-[bodyguard 1] Sir…

406
00:32:22,231 --> 00:32:23,441
[Emilia] Papa!

407
00:32:24,359 --> 00:32:25,485
Papa!

408
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:29,739
[Lily] You've lost, Julio Ardiente.

409
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:33,117
[in Spanish] Farewell, Grandpa!

410
00:32:33,451 --> 00:32:36,996
Call our lawyers! [gasps] Call our--

411
00:32:37,080 --> 00:32:38,164
Papa!

412
00:32:38,581 --> 00:32:40,959
How dare you! Papa!

413
00:32:42,043 --> 00:32:43,294
Papa!

414
00:32:43,378 --> 00:32:45,797
That's enough. Come on. Let's go. Get up.

415
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:47,173
[Emilia] Papa!

416
00:32:48,007 --> 00:32:49,008
[Raul] Let's go.

417
00:32:49,634 --> 00:32:51,594
[bodyguard 2] Hey, hey! Sir… Sir! Sir!

418
00:32:51,678 --> 00:32:52,929
Let's bring him to the hospital!

419
00:32:53,429 --> 00:32:54,681
[bodyguard 3] Governor! Governor!

420
00:32:54,764 --> 00:32:56,599
-Make way! Make way!
-Let's go!

421
00:32:58,059 --> 00:32:59,686
We aren't done yet!

422
00:32:59,769 --> 00:33:04,107
Cower in fear, Emilia,
because Lily Cruz has returned!

423
00:33:04,190 --> 00:33:06,317
[suspenseful music playing]

424
00:33:06,818 --> 00:33:08,152
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!
-[Raul] Arnaldo!

425
00:33:08,236 --> 00:33:09,779
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!
-[crowd exclaiming]

426
00:33:10,655 --> 00:33:13,449
[Raul] Arnaldo! Call a doctor!

427
00:33:13,783 --> 00:33:16,327
Call an ambulance!

428
00:33:16,411 --> 00:33:19,330
[Raul] Arnaldo, son! Call a doctor!

429
00:33:19,706 --> 00:33:22,291
[clamoring]

430
00:33:26,379 --> 00:33:27,839
[Emilia] Help us…

431
00:33:28,756 --> 00:33:32,844
[suspenseful music playing]

432
00:33:55,283 --> 00:33:57,785
[music fading]

433
00:33:59,579 --> 00:34:00,621
[Emilia] Arnaldo!

434
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:03,666
[Julio] Why isn't anyone listening to me?!

435
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:05,168
-I'm okay!
-Help them!

436
00:34:05,251 --> 00:34:07,336
-I'm fine!
-[Emilia] Doctor! Hurry up!

437
00:34:07,420 --> 00:34:09,672
You should look at my grandson
instead, please.

438
00:34:09,756 --> 00:34:12,091
-Let me get out of here.
-[Emilia] Please help Arnaldo!

439
00:34:12,175 --> 00:34:15,011
I'm starting to sound
like a broken record here!

440
00:34:15,094 --> 00:34:16,179
-My son…
-I'm okay!

441
00:34:16,262 --> 00:34:18,556
-Get me out of here! Come on!
-[doctor 1] Julio…

442
00:34:19,640 --> 00:34:21,267
I suggest that we do some tests

443
00:34:21,350 --> 00:34:24,353
so we know the cause of your chest pains.

444
00:34:24,437 --> 00:34:28,441
My chest hurts because
of that blasted Lily Cruz.

445
00:34:28,524 --> 00:34:31,194
-[Emilia] What's happening?!
-[Julio] Because of her lies!

446
00:34:31,277 --> 00:34:32,987
-Emilia, please…
-Doctor!

447
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:34,155
Julio, you have to…

448
00:34:34,238 --> 00:34:35,823
-[Emilia shrieking]
-You have to calm down, Julio.

449
00:34:35,907 --> 00:34:37,283
Get his blood pressure.

450
00:34:37,366 --> 00:34:38,618
-[Emilia] Nurse!
-[doctor 2] Nurse!

451
00:34:38,701 --> 00:34:40,078
-[Emilia] Nurse, come here!
-Emilia!

452
00:34:40,161 --> 00:34:43,289
-[doctor 1] You have to calm down.
-Get me Diazepam, one ampoule. Go!

453
00:34:43,372 --> 00:34:44,373
Faster!

454
00:34:45,416 --> 00:34:46,542
Doctor!

455
00:34:47,376 --> 00:34:49,003
Arnaldo! Papa?

456
00:34:49,796 --> 00:34:51,839
Papa! Is he okay, doctor?

457
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:53,633
He's going to be all right.
He's gonna be okay.

458
00:34:53,716 --> 00:34:55,384
Papa, wait, okay? Wait.

459
00:34:55,843 --> 00:34:57,804
Raul, don't just stand there!

460
00:34:57,887 --> 00:34:59,263
If you don't do anything,

461
00:34:59,347 --> 00:35:01,265
I'll have you wake up
in a hospital bed as well!

462
00:35:01,974 --> 00:35:03,643
Doctor, what is happening?! Come on!

463
00:35:03,726 --> 00:35:04,977
Arnaldo, son, please.

464
00:35:09,065 --> 00:35:11,567
[exhales sharply] Is he gonna be okay now?

465
00:35:11,651 --> 00:35:12,944
Your son is going to be okay.

466
00:35:13,277 --> 00:35:15,071
We just need to run some tests

467
00:35:15,154 --> 00:35:17,615
to find the cause of the seizure.

468
00:35:18,199 --> 00:35:20,118
-He's going to be fine.
-[Raul] Thank you, doctor.

469
00:35:20,201 --> 00:35:21,410
[doctor 2] He's going to be fine.

470
00:35:22,245 --> 00:35:25,873
[somber music playing]

471
00:35:27,708 --> 00:35:29,127
[sobbing]

472
00:35:33,131 --> 00:35:34,507
[nurse] Please make way.

473
00:35:34,590 --> 00:35:39,095
[somber music continues]

474
00:35:50,731 --> 00:35:53,442
Let's just wait for
the ombudsman's notification.

475
00:35:53,943 --> 00:35:56,112
Julio can still post bail,
but we are gunning

476
00:35:56,195 --> 00:35:58,156
for his indefinite suspension as governor.

477
00:35:58,239 --> 00:35:59,782
And if he's proven guilty,

478
00:35:59,866 --> 00:36:01,534
then he'll be banned from public office.

479
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:05,621
So if that happens, he can't run
for any position in government,

480
00:36:05,955 --> 00:36:09,667
be it district chairman
or president of the Philippines?

481
00:36:10,418 --> 00:36:12,295
Attorney, Vice Governor,

482
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:14,172
auntie, friends…

483
00:36:14,255 --> 00:36:15,923
thank you for all your help.

484
00:36:17,300 --> 00:36:18,801
And, of course, thank you, Ivy.

485
00:36:19,510 --> 00:36:21,971
The Ardientes wouldn't have
fallen if it weren't for you.

486
00:36:23,472 --> 00:36:24,974
We've finally taken back what's ours.

487
00:36:25,057 --> 00:36:27,977
We know that the Ardientes
are formidable enemies.

488
00:36:28,311 --> 00:36:31,189
But because we worked together
and didn't give up,

489
00:36:31,522 --> 00:36:34,859
those monsters no longer have their power.

490
00:36:35,526 --> 00:36:38,112
So thank you very much for all your help.

491
00:36:39,864 --> 00:36:43,576
I promise you, I will help
the citizens of Ardiente

492
00:36:43,659 --> 00:36:45,494
with the position you entrusted me.

493
00:36:46,454 --> 00:36:48,289
For a new Ardiente.

494
00:36:48,372 --> 00:36:49,999
For a new Ardiente.

495
00:36:50,082 --> 00:36:55,671
[reflective music playing]

496
00:37:11,771 --> 00:37:13,814
Doctor, how is my son?

497
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:15,399
Arnaldo is stable.

498
00:37:15,483 --> 00:37:17,068
The seizure was caused

499
00:37:17,151 --> 00:37:21,405
by an insufficient dosage
of his medication.

500
00:37:21,489 --> 00:37:24,533
This was indicated in
the results of his blood test.

501
00:37:24,992 --> 00:37:27,870
We will have to impose necessary steps

502
00:37:27,954 --> 00:37:30,122
to prevent this from happening again.

503
00:37:31,290 --> 00:37:33,751
What about Papa, doctor? How is he?

504
00:37:34,919 --> 00:37:36,837
Unfortunately, he's still unconscious.

505
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:38,589
But he's stable.

506
00:37:39,215 --> 00:37:41,384
We just have to give him
more time to recover.

507
00:37:42,468 --> 00:37:43,594
But he's okay.

508
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:46,764
[inaudible]

509
00:37:46,847 --> 00:37:50,393
[somber music playing]

510
00:38:08,452 --> 00:38:10,371
[sobbing]

511
00:38:12,206 --> 00:38:13,332
Papa…

512
00:38:14,917 --> 00:38:17,420
[Emilia sobbing]

513
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:21,841
Papa, wake up.

514
00:38:24,385 --> 00:38:26,887
Come on, you've got to wake up, Papa.

515
00:38:28,389 --> 00:38:29,598
[sobs]

516
00:38:30,516 --> 00:38:32,727
You have to wake up.

517
00:38:32,977 --> 00:38:35,646
You can't leave me yet, Papa.

518
00:38:39,317 --> 00:38:40,901
Papa, I know you.

519
00:38:42,486 --> 00:38:44,780
I know you're a fighter.

520
00:38:46,198 --> 00:38:48,159
When you wake up,

521
00:38:48,451 --> 00:38:50,661
and I know you will…

522
00:38:51,579 --> 00:38:55,166
because you'll force yourself to wake up.

523
00:38:57,626 --> 00:38:59,462
Come on. Wake up, Papa…

524
00:38:59,545 --> 00:39:01,922
[sobbing] Wake up!

525
00:39:05,051 --> 00:39:06,802
You can't die, Papa.

526
00:39:07,636 --> 00:39:09,805
You're an Ardiente.

527
00:39:11,307 --> 00:39:16,020
Weren't you the one who said
you'll live forever?

528
00:39:16,103 --> 00:39:17,563
So you can't die.

529
00:39:18,856 --> 00:39:20,524
I know you, Papa.

530
00:39:22,902 --> 00:39:26,781
I know you won't let
a nobody like Lily Cruz

531
00:39:26,864 --> 00:39:31,494
tarnish and ruin our family's reputation.

532
00:39:33,037 --> 00:39:36,749
That's why you can't die on me, Papa!

533
00:39:36,832 --> 00:39:38,667
[sobbing]

534
00:39:40,753 --> 00:39:44,757
Please, Papa…

535
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:47,176
[sobbing]

536
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:55,726
[melancholic music playing]

537
00:39:56,519 --> 00:39:59,438
[sobbing]

538
00:40:03,359 --> 00:40:04,443
Let's go.

539
00:40:11,826 --> 00:40:15,830
[pensive music playing]

540
00:40:17,123 --> 00:40:18,749
-<i>Mom, what happened to you?</i>
-[shushing]

541
00:40:18,833 --> 00:40:19,917
-<i>Hey!</i>
-[gasps]

542
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:22,128
<i>Lily! Run!</i>

543
00:40:26,424 --> 00:40:28,342
[tires screeching]

544
00:40:29,718 --> 00:40:31,178
<i>My mom?</i>

545
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:33,597
<i>My mom is alive.</i>

546
00:40:34,723 --> 00:40:35,766
<i>Mom?</i>

547
00:40:37,101 --> 00:40:38,227
<i>Mom!</i>

548
00:40:38,727 --> 00:40:40,521
<i>Mom! Mom!</i>

549
00:40:47,236 --> 00:40:48,237
<i>Mom!</i>

550
00:40:50,364 --> 00:40:53,409
<i>The Ardientes have broken us</i>
<i>again and again.</i>

551
00:40:54,034 --> 00:41:00,666
<i>Now, it's our turn to be whole</i>
<i>while they fall apart.</i>

552
00:41:01,709 --> 00:41:04,295
<i>Our family will be whole again, Mom.</i>

553
00:41:04,712 --> 00:41:08,090
<i>And we will never be broken again.</i>

554
00:41:08,174 --> 00:41:12,178
[pensive music playing]

555
00:41:26,108 --> 00:41:30,529
I'm sure Lily's happy now
that the Ardientes have fallen

556
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:32,907
and we have a new governor.

557
00:41:33,532 --> 00:41:36,494
I'm so happy for all of us.

558
00:41:38,496 --> 00:41:40,331
Diego, thank you so much.

559
00:41:41,123 --> 00:41:43,459
But still, Camia, don't let
your guard down.

560
00:41:44,251 --> 00:41:45,252
[sighs]

561
00:41:45,336 --> 00:41:49,381
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

562
00:41:55,763 --> 00:41:58,307
All right. Auntie, Diego,
I'm going upstairs.

563
00:41:58,390 --> 00:42:00,434
-Me too.
-All right. Good night, you two.

564
00:42:02,937 --> 00:42:04,438
Oh, Lily.

565
00:42:11,403 --> 00:42:12,738
Lily, dear.

566
00:42:12,821 --> 00:42:14,448
I thought you went home.

567
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:21,830
["Wildflower" instrumental swells]

568
00:42:36,428 --> 00:42:40,432
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

569
00:42:57,449 --> 00:43:01,954
["Wildflower" instrumental continues]

570
00:43:05,291 --> 00:43:06,542
[sobs]

571
00:43:08,961 --> 00:43:11,422
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]
<i>♪ Let her cry ♪</i>

572
00:43:11,505 --> 00:43:15,593
<i>♪ For she's a lady… ♪</i>

573
00:43:17,303 --> 00:43:20,472
-The governor's conscious now.
-Thank you, doctor.

574
00:43:20,931 --> 00:43:22,600
He's undergone oxygen therapy.

575
00:43:22,975 --> 00:43:24,852
I also prescribed some medication

576
00:43:24,935 --> 00:43:26,312
to prevent blood clotting,

577
00:43:26,395 --> 00:43:29,023
and to improve the blood flow
through the arteries.

578
00:43:29,523 --> 00:43:31,650
-[sighs] Thank you.
-He's going to be okay.

579
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:33,694
Thanks, doctor.

580
00:43:34,278 --> 00:43:35,237
You're welcome.

581
00:43:36,030 --> 00:43:39,575
[somber music playing]

582
00:43:45,205 --> 00:43:46,332
[sighs]

583
00:43:53,547 --> 00:43:56,216
[sobbing]

584
00:44:01,138 --> 00:44:04,433
Lily, I'll just fix my room.

585
00:44:04,516 --> 00:44:06,310
You can sleep there for the night.

586
00:44:07,144 --> 00:44:08,354
[inhales sharply]

587
00:44:09,772 --> 00:44:10,898
Mom…

588
00:44:16,945 --> 00:44:20,908
I don't want to sleep here
just for tonight.

589
00:44:23,577 --> 00:44:25,537
[voice shaking] If it's all right…

590
00:44:26,997 --> 00:44:29,208
I want to stay here for good.

591
00:44:33,462 --> 00:44:35,631
I want to live with you, Mom.

592
00:44:39,009 --> 00:44:40,177
Oh, Lily…

593
00:44:42,429 --> 00:44:45,766
I never thought this day would come.

594
00:44:46,016 --> 00:44:49,978
[soft piano music playing]

595
00:44:52,314 --> 00:44:54,066
But it's finally here.

596
00:44:57,736 --> 00:44:59,363
It's finally come, Mom.

597
00:45:00,781 --> 00:45:02,199
This is it.

598
00:45:03,242 --> 00:45:05,702
After everything we've been through,

599
00:45:06,036 --> 00:45:07,788
this day has finally come for us,

600
00:45:08,831 --> 00:45:10,791
we can now live together…

601
00:45:11,333 --> 00:45:13,127
because I'm finally free.

602
00:45:14,002 --> 00:45:18,132
Ivy Aguas is dead
and Lily Cruz is free again.

603
00:45:18,215 --> 00:45:21,051
Everyone knows that I'm Lily Cruz.

604
00:45:22,678 --> 00:45:25,764
We can finally live
under one roof again, Mom.

605
00:45:28,684 --> 00:45:31,145
I can be with my mother again.

606
00:45:31,228 --> 00:45:34,898
Yes, dear, now that we've won…

607
00:45:36,191 --> 00:45:38,569
embrace your victory.

608
00:45:38,652 --> 00:45:39,945
Hold it tight.

609
00:45:41,822 --> 00:45:44,324
Mom, this is my victory…

610
00:45:46,452 --> 00:45:49,371
To finally be with you.

611
00:45:50,330 --> 00:45:54,626
The two of us together,
along with everyone I love.

612
00:45:55,627 --> 00:45:57,921
This is my greatest victory, Mom.

613
00:46:00,924 --> 00:46:02,009
Mom.

614
00:46:04,595 --> 00:46:09,183
[soft piano music playing]

615
00:46:17,941 --> 00:46:18,984
Papa.

616
00:46:20,110 --> 00:46:22,738
Get me out of here, Emilia.

617
00:46:23,197 --> 00:46:24,281
Relax.

618
00:46:25,199 --> 00:46:28,827
The doctor said you're going
to be discharged tomorrow.

619
00:46:29,328 --> 00:46:31,163
And Attorney De Jesus called.

620
00:46:31,246 --> 00:46:32,873
He said he's taking care of your case

621
00:46:32,956 --> 00:46:34,583
so you can post bail.

622
00:46:37,085 --> 00:46:38,295
Aren't you glad?

623
00:46:39,546 --> 00:46:40,714
Glad?

624
00:46:41,965 --> 00:46:43,967
How can I be glad…

625
00:46:45,302 --> 00:46:49,431
knowing that the vermin
who caused the downfall

626
00:46:49,515 --> 00:46:52,893
of our family is still alive
and roaming freely out there?

627
00:46:53,227 --> 00:46:56,772
That damn Lily Cruz…

628
00:46:59,316 --> 00:47:02,736
Neither Ivy Aguas

629
00:47:02,819 --> 00:47:08,200
nor Lily Cruz--
or whatever name she's using--

630
00:47:08,909 --> 00:47:11,245
will bring me down.

631
00:47:12,538 --> 00:47:14,623
Does she actually think she's smart?

632
00:47:15,707 --> 00:47:19,294
Her followers are nothing but simpletons

633
00:47:20,295 --> 00:47:23,799
who believe whatever a populist says.

634
00:47:24,299 --> 00:47:25,384
[scoffs]

635
00:47:26,802 --> 00:47:29,888
They will never bring me down.

636
00:47:31,598 --> 00:47:33,350
Not them.

637
00:47:35,352 --> 00:47:40,274
So, do they think that their lives
are gonna be better

638
00:47:40,816 --> 00:47:44,236
in the hands of those amateurs?

639
00:47:45,862 --> 00:47:49,241
Damn. Just wait and see.

640
00:47:50,200 --> 00:47:56,081
Once I get out of this hospital
and post my bail,

641
00:47:56,957 --> 00:47:59,001
I will take back my rightful place.

642
00:47:59,668 --> 00:48:02,045
But, Papa, you shot Camia Cruz.

643
00:48:02,129 --> 00:48:03,422
So what?

644
00:48:03,505 --> 00:48:05,841
If I see that woman again,
I'll shoot her again.

645
00:48:07,467 --> 00:48:09,720
Papa, you can post your bail,

646
00:48:09,803 --> 00:48:13,932
but you can't return
to being a governor again.

647
00:48:15,183 --> 00:48:17,102
Papa, you're so doomed.

648
00:48:17,185 --> 00:48:19,104
You are so doomed.

649
00:48:20,188 --> 00:48:24,192
[tense music playing]

650
00:48:31,867 --> 00:48:34,536
<i>From this day forward, you will address me</i>

651
00:48:34,620 --> 00:48:36,580
<i>by my real name,</i>

652
00:48:36,663 --> 00:48:37,831
<i>Lily Cruz.</i>

653
00:48:38,665 --> 00:48:41,668
<i>What's more important to you?</i>
<i>Becoming the queen of Ardiente,</i>

654
00:48:41,752 --> 00:48:44,338
<i>or discovering your mom's identity?</i>

655
00:48:44,421 --> 00:48:47,132
<i>Both. I want to be the queen of Ardiente</i>

656
00:48:47,215 --> 00:48:52,846
<i>and have acting Governor Mateo Ruiz</i>
<i>at my beck and call.</i>

657
00:48:52,929 --> 00:48:54,181
[screams]

658
00:48:57,559 --> 00:49:00,687
<i>-Someone wants to see you.</i>
<i>-Who?</i>

659
00:49:01,647 --> 00:49:02,856
<i>Red Dragon.</i>

660
00:49:02,939 --> 00:49:04,983
[tense music playing]

661
00:49:05,067 --> 00:49:06,943
[theme music playing]
